Subject: Tweak: fast menus
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

With "Fast menus" enabled menu transitions are skipped, outside matches and
the boot screens. In a match its menus count too: the pause menu and the
screens it opens (Choose Sides, options, quit popup) while the pause menu
state is up (FrontEnd::m_bInPauseMenuState, issue #39), and the post-match
screens from its GameOver event (FrontEnd::m_bGameOver), which brings up the
results, the result popups and the stats. The match itself and its end
sequence keep their pace.

- 2D: one-shot slides no longer than 3 s jump to their end, and a screen's
  presentation starts a one-shot slide of up to 6 s at its end, as the game
  does for popups. Slides reset this frame keep their first frame; longer
  slides (credits) and looping ones keep their pace.
- 3D: while the front end's presentation runs a transition script outside a
  match, its scripted waits end as they start and its camera moves run 30
  times faster. Only the camera task (BeginFrameTask) runs on that
  transition time: no script waits for an effect, and effects at 30 times
  their speed advanced up to 3 s a frame, so most particles were removed
  before they were drawn and the rest popped in and out (issue #34).
  Effects, audio, rumble and pads keep real time; a match's tasks never run
  on transition time. A looping camera, a screen's idle view, keeps real
  time as well: camera blends keep their pace, and the Strikers Cup hub's
  60 s orbit of the trophy ran on through each 1.5-2 s blend into it and
  came to rest facing the trophy from another side (issue #49).
- Popups: the black box behind a popup, which FEPopupMenu grows itself over
  0.75 s rather than through a slide, opens at full size at once. A popup
  whose slide is already past 1 s when its layout hides the text shows it
  again.
- Quitting a match from the pause menu: once the quit popup has gone, the
  game returns to the front end at once instead of after the rest of the
  pause menu's 1 s wait (PauseMenuScene::mQuitDelay).

